// Native save / load end to end: resume parity with the Python prototype (resume.py via World.from_native_state), the four cases of
// re/interp/test_save.py, and a byte-for-byte comparison of a Swift-written save with the Python-written one for the same state.
// The expected digests were generated by running the Python code (`re/.venv/bin/python -I -W ignore`): `start` = canonical lines
// of the freshly resumed state (stateLines), `after300` = the same after 300 `vm.tick_once(); world.step()` frames plus the
// engine-side logs (runLines). The game files come from $BIOFORGE_DATA (GAMEDAT = its sibling folder).
// nativeResume.after300 was regenerated 2026-10-22: the two nurse hits on Lex (ticks 8 and 243) now run LEX_WOUNDS, whose engine calls
// (ISMYFORM, COUNTBITS, APPLY ...) enter the engine log; states and positions are unchanged. The log hash is over UTF-8 text (the
// SUBTITLE entries hold CP437 characters such as U+0082), so the Python digest is computed with .encode('utf-8').
// All four digests below changed on 2026-10-24 when COMPASS, HEADING, ISMYFORM, ISINCOMBATMODE, ISKEYPRESSED, AMINEXTENT and FLOATATHEIGHT were
// ported: CELL3_MON (CHAOSBLK) loops on `AMINEXTENT (CURFIG, CE3)`, which used to read 0 and now animates the cell indicators (and plays
// `_pim_beep_5`) while Lex is in CE3, so more processes / sound handles / VARS.DEF globals. Verified: the unchanged HEAD code reproduces the old
// digests exactly with the same Python generator, the new ones come from the new code.
// 2026-11-02 a motion's first update moves by frame 0's root (re/NOTES.md "Movement fixes"): nativeResume.after300 (Lex's RECOIL_ML and the nurse's first moves) and the new-game save's
// CHAOS.IFF / IM1 changed (`start`, the GAMEDAT digests and every other save file did not). Regenerated with the Python code; the generator reproduced the GAMEDAT digests and `start` first.
// 2026-11-02 LINKMETOCAMERAS pauses the processes linked to other cameras (re/NOTES.md "Camera-linked processes"): all four resume digests moved (the resumed bars, FLICKER_LIGHT,
// BLOCK_DRIP and the animations are paused on the saved camera), and the new-game save's files listed in that section. Regenerated with the Python code; the generator reproduced the old digests at HEAD first.
// 2026-11-02 every update's root move rounds down (re/NOTES.md "Root moves round down"): nativeResume.after300 and the new-game save moved with Lex and the nurse. Regenerated with the Python code; the generator reproduced the GAMEDAT digests and `start` first.
// 2026-11-02 the player returns to idle when a scripted motion ends (1088:4155): nativeResume.after300 moved. Regenerated with the Python code; the generator reproduced the GAMEDAT digests and `start` first.
// 2026-11-03 SOUND is one-shot (1028:09d3): a looped sample's handle now ends, so both after300 digests and the new-game save moved; `start` did not. Regenerated with the Python code.
// 2026-10-31 audio: ambient loops, OVERTIME ramps; opening +30 ticks: both after300 digests and the new-game save's VARS.DEF / IM1 changed (`start` did not).
// 2026-11-04 a level's floor items get their record's script locals (re/NOTES.md "Item charges"): all four resume digests moved. Regenerated with re/tools/resume_digest.py, which reproduced the old digests on the old code first.
// 2026-11-08 a save carries the running script processes, the figures' AI name / velocity / viewing cameras and the item order (re/NOTES.md "Save state"): all four digests
// moved (`start` too: a resumed figure keeps its AI name and velocity and is put in its area; the new game's SCRIPT.DAT / MISC.DAT / CHAOS.IFF / IM1). Regenerated with re/tools/resume_digest.py
// and re/tools/newgame_save_digest.py.
// 2026-11-08 a load makes the items in record order (FUN_1148_0d46; re/NOTES.md "The inventory order after a load"): gamedatResume moved, as the shipped GAMEDAT's
// floor items now come before Lex's. Regenerated with re/tools/resume_digest.py, which reproduced the old digests on the old code first.
// 2026-11-18 motion sound cues and the cutting sound-name lookup (re/NOTES.md "Motion sound cues and formatted sound names"): nativeResume.after300
// and the new-game save moved (more sound handles); `start` and the GAMEDAT digests did not. Regenerated with re/tools/resume_digest.py and
// re/tools/newgame_save_digest.py, which reproduced the old digests on the old code first.
// 2026-11-20 a waiter woken by a process's end runs in the next scheduler walk (re/NOTES.md "A woken waiter runs in the next walk"): nativeResume.after300 and
// the new-game save moved (CHAOS.IFF, IM1, LISTS.FLX, MISC.DAT, SCRIPT.DAT); `start` and the GAMEDAT digests did not. Regenerated with re/tools/resume_digest.py and
// re/tools/newgame_save_digest.py.
